From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: GammaOS's defaults for accurate multiplication, asynchronous shader
 builds and the right eye, as core options

azahar-nano on GammaOS runs Super Mario 3D Land at full speed on the same
RG52 Mini; this core ran it at half (30 emulated frames a second in 1-1,
Mali-G52 at 900 MHz busy 95% of the time). Three of the differences are
settings, and GammaOS's frontend has them so:

- Accurate multiplication off (its config default). On it cost 1.2 ms of the
  GPU's vertex work a frame there.
- Shaders built in the background (async_shader_compilation), so a scene
  with new shaders does not stop the game until they are built: the first
  run without accurate multiplication stood still over 80 s here.
- The right eye not drawn (disable_right_eye_render). With the 3D slider at
  zero the screen never shows it; Super Mario 3D Land draws it anyway, and
  it is half of the frame's GPU work.

The first changes its default; the other two become core options, both on.

